      en: ["Le Cesine was designated as a Ramsar site in 1977.", "The protected area covers approximately 380 hectares of land.", "The two main coastal ponds are named Salapi and Pantano Grande.", "More than 180 bird species have been documented in the oasis.", "The visitor center, Masseria Le Cesine, dates back to the 16th century.", "The name 'Cesine' comes from the Latin for 'felled trees' or 'clearings'."],
